# Walkthrough - EdLove Footer Implementation

I have successfully implemented the footer for the EdLove web application.

## Changes

### 1. New Footer Component
I created [src/components/Footer.astro](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/edlove-web/src/components/Footer.astro) which includes:
- **Brand Section**: "edlove.org" with a mission statement.
- **Navigation Links**: About Us, Privacy Policy, Terms of Use.
- **Contact Info**: `hello@edlove.org`.
- **Attribution**: "Built with 💖 by the EdLove Community".
- **Styling**: Used `deep-indigo` background and `warm-gold` accents to match the design system.

### 2. Layout Integration
I updated [src/layouts/Layout.astro](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/edlove-web/src/layouts/Layout.astro) to:
- Import the new `Footer` component.
- Add `min-h-screen` and `flex-col` structure to ensure the footer stays at the bottom of the page.
- Render the `<Footer />` at the end of the `<body>`.

## Verification Results

### Build Verification
Ran `npm run build` to ensure the Astro project compiles with the new component.

> [!NOTE]
> The footer links currently point to `/about`, `/privacy`, and `/terms`. These pages may need to be created in a future task if they don't exist yet.
